SolarDeck is dual-licensed by artifact type.

  Hardware  (hardware/, docs/mechanical content, enclosure CAD)  ->  CERN-OHL-S-2.0
  Software  (firmware/, src/, tools/, scripts/, config/, docs code)  ->  MIT

Full texts live in LICENSES/. Where a file's category is ambiguous, the license of the directory
above it applies (see LICENSES/PATHS.md).

Copyright (c) 2026 the SolarDeck contributors.

CERN-OHL-S-2.0 is a strongly reciprocal open-hardware license: you may build, modify and sell
SolarDeck hardware, but modified designs must be published under the same terms, and the source of
the design must be made available. If you need different terms, ask.

MIT is a permissive software license: use it, ship it, sell it, keep your changes private, just keep
the copyright notice.
